{
	"_doc": "The Cash Shop catalog and the Fortune each cash slot adds (spec #34, ADR 0003). items[]: id (the MapleStory item id), kind (equip | pet | pet_upgrade), price (NX), sn (Etc.wz/Commodity.img serial number, tier A; omitted for survivor-only items), requires (item ids that must all be owned), requires_any (at least one of these must be owned), two_handed (weapon covers only: fills the weapon and shield slots), name/desc/icon (survivor-only items; icon is a WZ path; real items take name and description from String.wz and the icon from their own img). Real prices are the OnSale Commodity.img listings (tier A). The base pet already includes Item Pouch (1812001) and Meso Magnet (1812000): they are not sold. Pet upgrades 1812002-1812005 and VAC need an owned pet. Cash equipment entries (kind equip, #117) are 116 curated unisex items (tier C selection) at their OnSale Commodity.img price and SN (tier A): 6-10 per slot, art exported by the asset manifest; the 3 two_handed covers are the vslot WpSi ones (tier C inference). An overall fills top and bottom; a two-handed weapon cover fills weapon and shield. The slot comes from id / 10000: 100 hat, 101 face, 102 eye, 103 earrings, 104 top, 105 overall, 106 bottom, 107 shoes, 108 gloves, 109 shield, 110 cape, 170 weapon cover.",
	"_slot_fortune": "Tier C: placeholder Fortune added by each filled cash slot, summing to 100 with all 11 slots filled. Computed live each round and never written into a character. The balance pass sets the numbers.",
	"slot_fortune": {
		"hat": 10, "face": 8, "eye": 8, "earrings": 6, "top": 10, "bottom": 10,
		"shoes": 9, "gloves": 9, "cape": 10, "weapon": 12, "shield": 8
	},
	"_pet": "Tier C (spec #34 / #119): the pet in the round simulation (PetSystem). pickup_radius: the base pet (Item Pouch and Meso Magnet included) collects every drop kind this close (px) to its centre, center_up above its feet; binocular_mult scales it with Binocular. follow_gap / follow_speed_mult: how it follows the player on the footholds with the player's own physics. teleport_distance, or lost_distance for lost_seconds: it teleports to the player. leash / fetch_dy: Wing Boots fetch resting drops within this far (sideways / vertically) of the player at fetch_speed_mult, walking to within fetch_gap, giving up after fetch_give_up s and pausing fetch_pause s. Auto HP Potion Pouch: below the HP ALERT, drinks on the same cooldown as the player (the Auto MP Potion Pouch went with MP, ADR 0006) (tier C: spec #237); no extra delay. jump_*/down_*/stuck_seconds: when the follow controller presses jump; it counts as stuck against a wall when it moved less than stuck_move_px in a tick. speed_stat_floor: the pet's speed stat is the player's, but never below this (the 100 % base). floor_tolerance: px within which a floor counts as the same floor as the player's (a pet is brought out beside the player only on one). This file is the only place the numbers live (PetSystem has no defaults).",
	"pet": {
		"pickup_radius": 60, "center_up": 15, "binocular_mult": 2.0,
		"follow_gap": 40, "beside_offset": 30, "follow_speed_mult": 1.1,
		"teleport_distance": 600, "lost_distance": 280, "lost_seconds": 3.0,
		"leash": 220, "fetch_dy": 80, "fetch_gap": 6, "fetch_speed_mult": 1.5, "fetch_give_up": 2.5, "fetch_pause": 2.0,
		"jump_min_rise": 20, "jump_max_rise": 70, "jump_reach_dx": 80, "down_min_drop": 20, "down_dx": 60,
		"stuck_seconds": 0.3, "stuck_move_px": 0.2, "speed_stat_floor": 100, "floor_tolerance": 2.0
	},
